**6.5.5 Per-Shop Spending Breakdown**

Below the progress bar, a horizontal bar chart (using Swift Charts)
shows each shop\'s share of the selected month\'s total spend. Bars are
coloured to match the shop\'s icon background colour. Tapping a bar row
highlights the shop and shows the exact amount in a tooltip.

**6.5.6 Burn-Rate Projection Chart**

A line chart projected over the remaining days of the selected month.
This chart is only visible when the selected month is the current month
AND a budget has been set.

-   X-axis: Days of the current month (1 → last day).

-   Y-axis: Cumulative spend in the user\'s locale currency.

-   Solid line: Actual cumulative spend up to today.

-   Dashed line: Projected cumulative spend from today to end of month,
    calculated using a linear regression over the last 7 days of
    spending (or all days in the month if fewer than 7).

-   Horizontal dashed budget line: Drawn at the budget amount as a
    reference.

-   Intersection annotation: If the projection line crosses the budget
    line before month-end, a labelled marker is shown at the crossing
    point with the text \"Est. budget exhausted: \[date\]\".

-   If the projection does not reach the budget before month-end, a
    positive label is shown: \"Budget sufficient for full month\".

Projection Formula: The average daily spend rate is calculated as
total_spend / days_elapsed. The projected exhaustion date =
current_date + (remaining_budget / avg_daily_rate). This calculation
updates each time a new expense is saved.

