**8. Non-Functional Requirements**

**8.1 Performance**

-   Cold launch time (from tap to interactive home screen): ≤ 1.5
    seconds on an iPhone 12 or newer.

-   Grid scroll frame rate: ≥ 60 fps on all supported devices (≥ 120 fps
    on ProMotion devices).

-   Expense save-to-badge-update latency: ≤ 300ms.

-   Chart render time: ≤ 500ms after month selection change.

**8.2 Reliability**

-   All data is persisted to SwiftData (or Core Data) on the main thread
    with proper context saving. Data must survive app termination and
    device restart.

-   Crash-free session rate target: ≥ 99.5%.

-   No data loss on app background / foreground transitions.

**8.3 Accessibility**

-   Full Dynamic Type support across all text elements (minimum
    .caption2, maximum .accessibilityExtraExtraExtraLarge).

-   VoiceOver labels on all interactive elements (buttons, badges,
    charts).

-   Minimum tap target size: 44×44pt per Apple HIG.

-   Supports both Light and Dark Mode (system and manual override).

-   Colour is never the sole means of conveying information (e.g.
    progress bar also shows percentage text).

**8.4 Security & Privacy**

-   No network requests in v1.0; all data remains on-device.

-   No user account or PII collected.

-   App data is stored in the app\'s sandboxed container and is included
    in iCloud Backup by default.

-   Sensitive financial data excluded from iCloud Backup if user opts in
    to privacy mode (v1.1 consideration).

**8.5 Internationalisation**

-   Currency formatting uses NumberFormatter with .currencyStyle and the
    device locale.

-   Date formatting uses DateFormatter with .medium style and device
    locale.

-   All string literals extracted to Localizable.strings; English (en)
    as base locale for v1.0.

