**11. Key User Flows**

**11.1 Create a New Shop**

1.  User opens app → Shops tab displayed (empty state or grid).

2.  User taps + in navigation bar → Add Shop sheet slides up to .medium
    detent.

3.  User types shop name → Icon suggestion row populates in real time.

4.  User selects preferred icon from suggestions row (or taps More
    Icons...).

5.  User selects background colour from presets or custom picker.

6.  Save button becomes enabled; user taps Save.

7.  Sheet dismisses with animation; new shop cell animates into the
    grid.

**11.2 Log an Expense**

8.  User taps a shop cell in the grid → Shop Detail screen pushed.

9.  User taps + in navigation bar → Add Expense sheet presented.

10. User enters amount, optionally changes date, optionally enters note.

11. User taps Save → sheet dismissed; expense appears in list.

12. Badge on shop cell in grid updates to reflect new monthly total.

**11.3 Set Monthly Budget & View Projection**

13. User taps Analytics tab → current month selected by default.

14. Monthly summary card shows total spend; budget prompt visible.

15. User taps Set Budget → small sheet appears with numeric input.

16. User enters budget amount and taps Save.

17. Progress bar animates to reflect spend vs. budget.

18. Burn-rate projection chart appears below progress bar with actual +
    projected lines.

19. If projection crosses budget line: annotation shows estimated
    exhaustion date.

**11.4 View a Past Month**

20. User is on Analytics tab.

21. User taps the month selector (e.g. \"March 2025\").

22. Month picker opens; months with data are selectable, others dimmed.

23. User selects a past month → all analytics data refreshes for that
    month.

24. Burn-rate projection chart is hidden for past months (historical
    data only).

